<title>NORWAY: Saga's Tordis oilfield returns to normal output.</title>
<headline>Saga's Tordis oilfield returns to normal output.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oil production at the North Sea Tordis oilfield was normal on Friday following a brief scheduled maintenance shutdown, operator Saga Petroleum ASA said on Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;We restarted production Wednesday afternoon and were back to normal levels on Thursday,&quot; a spokesman for the company said.</p>
<p>Output was around 12,000 cubic metres per day, or 75,000 barrels per day, he said.</p>
<p>The field, which feeds crude to the Gullfaks C platform for processing and loading on to shuttle tankers, was shut down last Friday.</p>
<p>--Tanya Pang, Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
